    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><strong>Causal Spine Trace.</strong> You can follow a single spine of cause and effect through otherwise chaotic Lore.</p><ul><li>When you investigate a <strong>major campaign event</strong> (a war, a hex’s fall, a Spark drift, a faction coup), you can spend an hour performing a ritual analysis: timelines drawn on walls, string on maps, or a thousand-yard stare.</li><li>Make an <strong>Occult (Mind), Lore (Mind), or Investigation (Mind)</strong> check (GM sets DC). On a success, you identify the <strong>primary causal spine</strong>: the 2–3 key decisions, entities, or hexes that drove the outcome.</li><li>This gives the GM explicit permission to hand you a <strong>story skeleton</strong> you can attack: those become the levers for future refactors.</li></ul>",
